1
00:00:01,450 --> 00:00:10,000
Long, long ago, in the city of Susa, there lived a very powerful king. His name was King Xerxes.

2
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:17,580
The king chose a beautiful, kind young woman to be his queen. Her name was Esther.

3
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:25,990
Make way for the great Lord Haman!

4
00:00:26,690 --> 00:00:30,490
Hail, Lord Haman!

5
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:40,980
Ho ho! Did you see that? Everyone bows when I walk by! I'm the greatest man in the whole kingdom! Ha ha ha ha!

6
00:00:41,610 --> 00:00:46,890
But one man would not bow. Mordecai said, "I bow only to God."

7
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:54,800
What?! He won't bow to ME?! Grrr! Hmph! Hmph! Hmph!

8
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:07,740
O king... there are some people who don't keep your laws. Why not... let me get rid of them?

9
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:14,630
Hmm... very well. Take my ring. Do as you see fit.

10
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:18,530
Heh heh heh... Now nobody can stop me!

11
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:26,900
Esther, you must ask the king to save us! Maybe this is why you became queen, for a time just like this!

12
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:31,760
But... anyone who goes to the king without being called could die...

13
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:45,000
All right. Please pray for me. I will go to the king, even if it's dangerous!

14
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:53,360
Step by step, Esther climbed the palace stairs... What would the king do?

15
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:07,000
Queen Esther! You've come. What is it you want? Even half my kingdom, it's yours!

16
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:12,010
My king, will you come to my banquet? And bring Haman too.

17
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:20,800
The queen's banquet! Only the king... and ME! Ha! Aren't I wonderful!

18
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:26,230
Haman, there is a man I want to honour. What should I do for him?

19
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:30,290
Heh heh... who could that be, but me?

20
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:40,810
Dress him in the royal robe! Sit him on the king's own horse! And have someone shout: "This is the man the king honours!"

21
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:44,630
Good idea! Now go and do all of that for Mordecai!

22
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:50,060
Mor... Mor... MORDECAI?!

23
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:56,720
So Haman had to lead Mordecai through the city on the king's horse, shouting all the way...

24
00:02:58,270 --> 00:03:02,940
This... is the man the king honours... hmph!

25
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:11,130
My king... someone wants to destroy me, and all my people!

26
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:14,480
What?! Who is he? Who would dare?

27
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:18,330
It's him! This wicked man, Haman!

28
00:03:19,330 --> 00:03:26,470
No, no, no! My queen, save me! Oh king, have mercy!

29
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:28,820
Guards! Take him away!

30
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:37,770
Nooo! Let me go! I'm a very important man! I'm... waaaah!

31
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:48,510
The king had Haman taken away. God's people were saved! Everyone sang and danced for joy!

32
00:03:50,590 --> 00:03:56,770
Esther was scared, but she chose to be brave and to trust God. You can too!
